      "name": "Sticky Mock Data"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Path 1: n8n loops for you\n\nNo loop node here. The If node runs once and evaluates all five items, sending each one down the true or false branch. This is how most multi-item processing should be built.\n\nCheck the item counts on each branch after running.",
        "height": 300,
        "width": 520,
        "color": 5
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        176,
        384
      ],
      "id": "245e69b2-8afa-4e24-b50a-156c7140cf44",
      "name": "Sticky Implicit"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Path 2: when you need an explicit loop\n\nBatch size is 2, so this runs three times. Output 1 (loop) feeds the batch into Tag With Batch Number, which connects back into the loop node. Without that return wire the loop never iterates.\n\nOutput 0 (done) fires once at the end with all five items collected.",
        "height": 360,
        "width": 520,
        "color": 3
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
